#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:5
#: 904a96f698b246e69c8906cc42d74d37
msgid "Refining Calibration Parameters using a Flight Log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:7
#: deb3ebe3571743109d9afdf4fcd1326b
msgid "The compass offsets, scales, diagonals, and even motor compensation can be determined from a flight dataflash log of the vehicle using the web browser-based WebTools MagFit utility. This utility is available `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/WebTools/MAGFit/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:9
#: bd284528b38c4ae0a123af46caddcf1b
msgid "Using a flight log, the utility uses the GPS location, the vehicle attitude, and the World Magnetic Model database to compare the logged magnetic field components from the vehicle compass and compare the x/y/z values to that expected which are graphed. It also will run a calibration routine to correct the Ardupilot compass parameter values to improve the compass performance. Offsets (OFS), diagonals(DIA), ellipticals(ODI), motor current compensation, and scale parameters can be corrected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:12
#: df07a63aeb4d4563add0c1adfbb859e5
msgid "It can detect incorrect orientation, also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:15
#: c1b193b2b33a49ca88d0b32e1c61f093
msgid "Using WebTools MagFit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:16
#: 2d7cca9b0a73498aabbebe5dace721c5
msgid "load flight log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:17
#: 366b53cda297426a911e62904dfcdb85
msgid "select relevant portion of log to analyze (eliminate on the ground portions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:18
#: b9a7024d158d406b86c887536ae3fdd8
msgid "select which parameters to optimize( unless there is significant motor current interference or large nearby ferro-magnetic objects like batteries to the compass, offset optimization  will usually be sufficient)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:19
#: d5196259131b404591384719c79f219a
msgid "check if the reduction in heading deviation is acceptable with the new param values(usually <10deg is okay)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:20
#: 48ec43e26e1d4984a49534a32b7c7f4f
msgid "save the new values to a file and load into the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:22
#: e785adffe84a4a99a4323eb7e5380e25
msgid "Here is a video explaining the utility's options and use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:28
#: ce49acece1424480a9b17e7f5cc27843
msgid "Using MAVExplorer's integrated Magfit utility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:30
#: 26465157fc7a4357af91a24b68672b98
msgid "Now MAVExplorer has a Tools menu which includes this utility and allows it to be applied to any portion of the log by simply opening any Graph and zooming (magnifying glass icon) to the area to be analyzed. If no graph is opened, and area selected, then the entire log will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:32
#: 67c5bcd8fc5a4cbca71fd64b9affe610
msgid "Below is a video of the process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:34
#: 28bfe67579bf441583e54ecf4826f6cd
msgid "selecting CMOT No Change box, will calculate the CMOT correction values, but not apply them to the corrected graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:40
#: cf4ce58f2acc4fc6bfee475af6685c27
msgid "Hints and Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:42
#: dc0fc35592814cbe838b70d5f6060277
msgid "Be sure you have several complete turns during the flight and at least a few minutes of log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:43
#: ab23670d2aa34a42ae896cb7dc985fba
msgid "Be sure you put conditions on the analysis so you do not include data while on the ground or being carried."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:44
#: fadcd87389c64cac9d8f786fa28d36ad
msgid "Be sure you have already calibrated the compasses prior to the flight. You can use the tool on very poorly calibrated compasses, but that could be a flight hazard (unless its a plane or vehicle not dependent on compass)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:45
#: a668d37e562344cdb6cd4c79d46d99b3
msgid "If you have large COMPASS_MOT values indicating strong motor/battery system interference, be sure that none of those components can shift in flight, resulting in invalidating the compass motor interference corrections you entered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-magfit.rst:46
#: 58a27bad724c4efbbb7b6940a1c53238
msgid "The EKF's sole purpose is to filter out sensor inaccuracies and system disturbances. If the ATT yaw change is very large( > 20 degrees), this means that something else is possibly very wrong in the other sensors, or vehicle setup, and needs to be investigated before using the new compass calibration parameter values."
msgstr ""
